% Apparel rulings of U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CROSS, rulings.cbp.gov)
% run through the apparel model (apparel.le, which includes gri.le).
%
% One scenario per ruling; each style is described by the facts the ruling
% states, each fact citing the ruling ("as stated in ruling NY N362700"); the
% office's judgments carry who made them and why. The ruling's own code is NOT
% a fact: the expectation is the six-digit subheading the model derives, and
% where it differs from the ruling's the comment says so (DISAGREES) and why.
% Selection: the most recent rulings returned by CROSS for each of the
% subheadings 6105.10-20, 6106.10-20, 6109.10-90, 6110.20-90, 6205.20,
% 6206.30-40 (September 2026), keeping every style of each ruling. See
% README.md for the method and the results.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base apparel cbp includes these resources:
    apparel.

the knowledge base apparel cbp includes:

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% NY N362700 (July 2026): men's upper body garments from Jordan.
scenario ny_n362700 is:
    style 1025AD is an upper body garment, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD is classified under the US tariff, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    the fabric construction of style 1025AD is knitted, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    the cut of style 1025AD indicates men, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD has an opening starting at the neckline, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD has a collar, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD is napped, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD contains 92 percent of polyester, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD contains 8 percent of spandex, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1025AD is claimed to belong to outerwear, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    the claim that style 1025AD belongs to outerwear is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N362700,
        because "the garment lacks the character of an outerwear jacket designed for wear over all other clothing for protection against the elements".
    style 1000AD is an upper body garment, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1000AD is classified under the US tariff, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    the fabric construction of style 1000AD is knitted, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    the cut of style 1000AD indicates men, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1000AD has an opening starting at the neckline, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1000AD has a collar, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1000AD is napped, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1000AD contains 100 percent of polyester, as stated in ruling NY N362700.
    style 1000AD has pockets below the waist,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N362700,
        because "on a mannequin a portion of each side seam pocket is below the waist; per HQ H293112, if any part of a pocket is below the waist it is a pocket below the waist".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style 1025AD is 6105.20",
        "the subheading of style 1000AD is 6110.30"].

% The request of NY N362700 before CBP answered it: the importer claims that
% style 1025AD is an outerwear jacket of heading 6101, and nobody has decided.
% The model's answer is conditional on that judgment — the judgment needed is
% the unknown.
scenario request_n362700 is:
    style 1025AD is an upper body garment, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    style 1025AD is classified under the US tariff, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    the fabric construction of style 1025AD is knitted, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    the cut of style 1025AD indicates men, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    style 1025AD has an opening starting at the neckline, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    style 1025AD has a collar, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    style 1025AD contains 92 percent of polyester, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    style 1025AD contains 8 percent of spandex, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    style 1025AD is claimed to belong to outerwear, according to the importer, as stated in the request of NY N362700.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style 1025AD is 6105.20"]
        and unknowns ["the claim that style 1025AD belongs to outerwear is rejected"].

